# Visual language

Quiet editorial page: generous type, little chrome, set like a résumé. Light and dark are both finished. Define every color in both themes together.

## Type

- Latin `h1–h6`: Source Serif 4, weight 600, solid `text-foreground`, normal tracking. Load the face in `src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx` when restyling.
- `html[lang="ar"] h1–h6`: Noto Sans Arabic, weight 700.
- Body and UI: Inter. Arabic body stays Noto Sans Arabic.

## Layout

- Experience, Skills, Projects, and Contact share one vertical padding. Headings and body in those sections are `text-start`.
- The hero name block is the only centered region.

## Color and surface

- One accent: a near-foreground ink, not a saturated violet. Use it for links, focus, and one primary action.
- Surfaces are solid `bg-background` or `bg-card` with a 1px `border-border`. Light is paper. Dark is near-black.
- Tags, dates, and skill names are plain text or a neutral border.

## Motion

- Animate color and opacity only, at most 200ms.
- Keep the `prefers-reduced-motion` block in `src/app/globals.css`.

## Banned treatments

Gradient text, glass, backdrop blur, radial glows, grid masks, blur orbs, `font-black`, `tracking-tighter`, primary-tinted pills, hover scale, ping dots, spring easings, and scroll-reveal on every block.

```tsx
// Bad
<h2 className="text-gradient font-black tracking-tighter">

// Good
<h2 className="font-serif text-foreground">
```
